nowline v1

// Narrow-column labels under a bounded recurrence (specs/working-calendar.md
// §7.2). Summer Fridays take every Friday out from Jul 1 to Aug 31, so each
// week from Jun 29 to Aug 24 has four working days and its column is 32 px
// under the default `non-working:hide`, too narrow for a 35 px "Jun 29".
//
// The stressed axis is the week tick labels:
//   - Inside the recurrence the nine narrowed weeks form one run, so their
//     labels alternate (Jul 06, Jul 20, Aug 03, Aug 17), each one borrowing
//     half of the unlabelled column on either side. Before the fix every
//     label in the run was dropped and the axis was blank for nine weeks.
//   - Juneteenth (Fri Jun 19) narrows one week between two full ones. A lone
//     narrowed week keeps the plain rule: its label is dropped.
// The recurrence has a title but is not labelled on the chart (only dated
// declarations are), so the axis is the only place the stretch shows.

config

non-working juneteenth "Juneteenth" date:2026-06-19

non-working fridays "Summer Fridays" every:fri start:2026-07-01 end:2026-08-31

roadmap non-working-recurrence "Summer Fridays" start:2026-06-01 scale:1w calendar:business

anchor kickoff "Kickoff" date:2026-06-01
swimlane platform "Platform"
  item api-v2 "API v2" duration:4w
  item data-migration "Data migration" duration:6w
  item hardening "Hardening" duration:4w
